  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I found the main reason your laptop is slow. Its drive is almost full, with only about 9 GB (3.5%) free. Windows needs at least 10% free space to run smoothly. Here's how to free up space:\n\n1. Empty your Recycle Bin and clear out your Downloads folder.\n2. Go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files. Remove temporary files and old Windows Update files.\n3. Turn on OneDrive Files On-Demand. Your synced files will then stay in the cloud until you open them.\n4. Uninstall any apps you no longer use.\n5. Do a full restart from the Start menu. Closing the lid doesn't count.\n6. After that, install any pending Windows updates and restart again.\n\nIf it's still slow after this, or Windows says space is still low, reply to this ticket. Please also let us know if it started after an update or a new app install. We'll check whether the laptop needs a bigger drive or more help.",
  "internal_note": "User Leo Martins (id 6, Sales) owns BL-LT-0106 (Win 11 Pro, online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:42 UTC). Device status shows 9.0 GB free out of 256 GB (3.5%), with a low disk space warning. This matches the KB-017 threshold (<10%) and is the likely cause of the slowness under KB-019. Sent the user the KB-017 cleanup steps and the KB-019 restart/updates steps. No action tools needed. Next step if the user replies: re-run check_device_status to confirm free space. Escalate per KB-017/KB-019 if it stays under 10% after cleanup or the laptop is still slow after restart and updates (may need a larger drive or replacement).",
